title: AskAboutSalem
---
"So," You started. The server looked at you while she. Looking up, she was currently wiping down the counter even when it still looked spotless "Are you in uni?"
Her wiping slowed before she looked back at the counter "I am actually!" she said, sounding very happy as she did "Im a student here, so its convenient that I work here," she ended what she said with a giggle.
From there you asked her more questions about herself. She seemed more than happy to share more information about herself to you, and her eyes seemed more relaxed the more you spoke.
Eventually, your cup became empty and your brownie was in your stomach, and you were nice and full.
===

title: AskAboutWeather
---
You sat down at an empty chair, placing your tray of goods on the table. The atmosphere was suddenly quiet and you felt that you should say something. “Nice weather we’re having huh?” You said to pass the time, biting into the brownie. The server looked up form what she was doing, which was wiping down the counter, and she blinked in what seemed like confusion. 
You also blinked back, wondering why she wasn’t saying anything, before looking out the window. It was raining. Hard. Ah…so that’s why. “It’s raining…,” she said bluntly, and you sighed and cringed. Yeah…you already knew.
 “Nice for uh the plants,” you added on despite the embarrassment, and she just smiled and nodded. So much for making it less awkward, you just made it worse.
===

title: EatYourFood
---
You sat down at an empty chair, placing your tray of goods on the table. The atmosphere was suddenly quiet and you felt that you should say something. You thought about what to say and…nothing. You had an inkling you’d ruin the atmosphere so you sat there silently and ate your food. 
===

title: LookingBack
---
Looking back at her as you sat in your chair, you contemplated whether or not to ask her to be apart of your candidates. There was no limits on who you could ask, so you decided why not.
You approached the counter again after you were done with your food and she saw you waiting. Washing her hands and drying them off, she came over, showing you a kind smile once more "Hi dear, did you want to order more?" She asked, and you shook your head.
"Hi, I was just wondering," You had started after a weird period of silence. She had stood up straighter at that, turning fully to face you "My name is Y/n. I need some volunteers for my last essay in Philosophy, and I was wondering if you'd be interested in being one,"
She tilted her head, blinking at you as she considered your words. "Okay!" she cheerfully "I'll join,"You smiled happily and gave her the first question you needed, explaining what it was for. She had nodded eagerly, and you bid her a goodbye.
She seemed nice.
===